erts 7% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: a Piotroski score of 7/9.","ROE of 2% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.5x equity multiplier).","It spends 5.5% of revenue on R&D and 0.7% on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 2.6x net debt to EBITDA ($1.9B of cash against $7.6B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 3.3x."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 5.3% over 3 years, 9.3% over 5 years and 3.0% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating.","At current returns, reinvesting 100% of profits supports about 10.4% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 13.0% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.00, a backlog worth 1% of annual revenue and deferred revenue down 27%.","Capex runs only 0.7x depreciation (3.2% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 16, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.9%), and institutions hold 99%.","Insider trading is two-way: 7 purchases and 2 sales over the past year, net $8.2M bought.","It returns 5.1% a year to shareholders (5.1% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 5.5% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 140,000 employees, each generates about $146K of revenue, 0.4x the Consumer Cyclical median, and revenue has grown 2.1% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $11K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $4.1M (28x revenue per employee)."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":80,"head":"Invest: trades 74% below fair value of $149; revenue grew 9.3%/yr over 5y.","pros":["Composite 54, above the 39 line (gates 18/26)","Trades 74% below fair value of $149","Revenue grew 9.3%/yr over 5y","Piotroski F-score 7/9","P/E 10.8x vs sector 18.8x"],"cons":["12-1 month momentum -45%"],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_b